    <main class="main">
      <h1>Installation Guide</h1>

      <p>The <strong>2026.08.04 test version</strong> passed full install testing (first-party software installs cleanly, signed repository available) and is the current usable test release. Download and distribution details are at <a href="https://github.com/Linxira-OS/linxira-iso/releases" target="_blank">linxira-iso GitHub Releases</a>; the public release is planned to follow. Below is the complete installation process.</p>

      <h2>Download the ISO</h2>
      <p>Test ISO filename <code>linxira-2026.08.04-x86_64.iso</code> (~4.5GB, SHA-256 <code>f5d18f0dc7d25fd2944509ec51b9c4097ab6fab1444c7d591e3dc3e28d030708</code>). Verify the SHA-256 before installing to ensure file integrity.</p>

      <h2>Creating Bootable Media</h2>
      <h3>Windows</h3>
      <p>Use <a href="https://rufus.ie/" target="_blank">Rufus</a> or <a href="https://etcher.balena.io/" target="_blank">balenaEtcher</a>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Insert a USB drive with at least 8 GB of space</li>
        <li>Open Rufus</li>
        <li>Select the downloaded ISO file</li>
        <li>Select your USB device</li>
        <li>Click "Start"</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Linux</h3>
      <p><code>sudo dd if=linxira-*.iso of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress</code></p>

      <h2>Planned Installer</h2>
      <p>The Direct Arch Live image boots into a complete Plasma desktop and opens Linxira Welcome automatically. Calamares does not auto-start: launch it manually from Welcome or the application menu when you are ready. The expected flow is:</p>
      <ol style="color:#94a3b8; margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.5rem;">
        <li>Boot from the USB drive</li>
        <li>Open "Install Linxira OS" in Welcome or the application menu</li>
        <li>Choose your language and keyboard layout</li>
        <li>Select a partitioning scheme. <code>btrfs</code> with Timeshift is recommended.</li>
        <li>Choose optional reviewed profiles from catalog v2 and create your user account</li>
        <li>Wait for the installer to finish</li>
        <li>Restart the system and remove the USB drive</li>
      </ol>
      <p>After first boot, use Shelly for graphical package management. Shelly is not an installer dependency and does not perform Calamares transactions.</p>

      <h2>System Requirements</h2>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Component</th><th>Minimum</th><th>Recommended</th></tr>
        <tr><td>CPU</td><td>64-bit x86</td><td>4+ cores</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Memory</td><td>4 GB</td><td>8+ GB</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Storage</td><td>20 GB</td><td>50+ GB</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Graphics</td><td>OpenGL 2.0 support</td><td>Dedicated NVIDIA or AMD GPU</td></tr>
      </table>
    </main>
